1. Prefer coroutineScope Over Manual launch

Use the coroutineScope suspending builder for parallel work.
It automatically waits for all internal children to finish.
It destroys children if any sibling throws an exception.

// LEAK-FREE: Naturally scoped, blocks return until all tasks finish
suspend fun fetchDashboardData(): Dashboard = coroutineScope {
    val user = async { repository.getUser() }
    val news = async { repository.getNews() }
    Dashboard(user.await(), news.await())
}



2. Never Use GlobalScope

GlobalScope operates completely outside structured concurrency.
It keeps tasks alive even if your UI or screen is destroyed.
Replace it with class-level, lifecycle-bound scopes.

// BAD: Leaks memory if the caller drops the reference
GlobalScope.launch { doHeavyWork() }

// GOOD: Bound to a controlled lifecycle scope
class MyManager(private val scope: CoroutineScope) {
    fun start() = scope.launch { doHeavyWork() }
}


3. Clean Resources inside finally

Cancellation triggers a CancellationException inside the coroutine.
Always release heavy objects or listeners inside a finally block.

scope.launch {
    try {
        registerExpensiveListener()
        delay(10000)
    } finally {
        // This ALWAYS runs, even during cancellation, preventing leaks
        unregisterExpensiveListener()
    }
}

4. Collect Flows Safely on Android

Regular flow.collect() keeps running even if the app goes to the background.
Use repeatOnLifecycle or flowWithLifecycle to stop collection.
This automatically destroys the collector coroutine when the UI stops.

lifecycleScope.launch {
    // Automatically cancels collection when UI stops, releasing memory
    myFlow.flowWithLifecycle(lifecycle, Lifecycle.State.STARTED)
        .collect { data -> updateUI(data) }
}


5. Check isActive in CPU-Heavy Loops

Cancellation is cooperative; a tight loop can ignore cancellation.
If a coroutine cannot stop, it holds onto all its captured variables.
Insert ensureActive() or check isActive inside loops.

scope.launch(Dispatchers.Default) {
    while (isActive) { // Keeps the loop cooperative with structured cancellation
        processNextChunk()
    }
}
